-- and the other side, which the earlier theorem got wrong: two reports on one species whose values
-- disagree, together with one function agreeing with both -- the function being the count itself, and what
-- reconciles them being that their situations differ. A record that cannot tell this case from the
-- Inventory's is a record whose disagreements cannot be read in either direction: it will call a
-- temperature series a contradiction and a contradiction a difference of conditions.
sr-cyh-consistent : (a : sr-value Nat sr-cyh-room ≡ sr-value Nat sr-cyh-cold → Empty) × ((b : count-in (sr-species Nat sr-cyh-room) (sr-situation Nat sr-cyh-room) ≡ sr-value Nat sr-cyh-room) × (count-in (sr-species Nat sr-cyh-cold) (sr-situation Nat sr-cyh-cold) ≡ sr-value Nat sr-cyh-cold))
sr-cyh-consistent = (sr-cyh-disagree , (sp-cyh-room , sp-cyh-cold))
